# ledger.jsonl is NOT ignored. It is tracked: it is the oracle's witness log,
# and a scorer that cannot remember must not be able to report green.
#
# What IS ignored is the LOCAL ledger. `oracle.mjs watch` writes to
# ledger.local.jsonl, because a machine with no sibling checkouts writes a row
# where every port is "unknown" and every suite is "missing" -- which
# `summarise` would then read as version drift on every port. The witness log
# must hold runs, not the shape of a laptop.
ledger.local.jsonl
